o was gruesomely  killed and  we know emmett till was racially  motivated we're not so sure here but it  could have been  you know as far as the civil case i  think there are reasons to bring a  wrongful death action  she's claiming the mother is that she  reported him missing one day and yet  nothing was done for days after the fact  and the sheriff is disputing exactly the  date he was reported missing  and also whether an amber alert should  have been made here so she has grounds i  think  for bringing a wrongful death and maybe  even a civil rights claim  now imran all of that's really  interesting because as i understand it  the local police never notified state  police  and it's the state police who actually  have the power to issue an amber alert  the police also didn't report his  disappearance to local media  the family is placing the blame of  kwaiwan's death squarely at the police's  feet  what do you think yeah brian that's um  in my opinion a little problematic for  the police i think there could have been  a break-in procedure there may be a  procedure when someone is  missing particularly a child on the  local level  that wasn't followed and we know that  the state police did not get that amber  alert out there  because they were not notified it also  may lead to some changes in some  legislation  locally down there perhaps they're going  to give the local police the authority  to issue an amber alert but i think it's  pretty pretty uh interesting  um regarding that interplay and that may  be the grounds for a civil suit  absolutely thank you both when we come  back remembering larry flint  the media mogul the scandal the lawsuits  and the legacy  a judge presiding over the george floyd  case has denied the state's request to  reinstate  third degree murder charges against the  four former minneapolis police officers  derek shovin was initially charged with  third degree murder and is now facing  two charges of second-degree  manslaughter  and second-